   $q$A formal essay contains these sentences: "The printing press spread ideas faster than ever before. You could suddenly buy a book for way less money." Which revision of the second sentence keeps the essay's style consistent?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Books suddenly became far more expensive to buy.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-meaning"},{"text":"You could suddenly buy a book for much less money.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"shifts-to-second-person"},{"text":"Books suddenly became far less expensive to buy.","is_correct":true},{"text":"People could suddenly snag a book for way less cash.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Books suddenly became far less expensive to buy.$q$, $q$The correct choice removes both the shift to "you" and the casual "way less," matching the third person style of the first sentence. "For much less money" fixes the slang but still addresses the reader as "you."$q$, 'draft', null)
