values ('208778e9-eda2-5ea7-bd39-41e7bfa0a4e1', 'wg10-writing-with-evidence-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Draft: Rowing in Time$q$, $q$(1) In Rosa Delgado's short story "The Long Stroke," a ninth grader named Mei joins her school's rowing team expecting to win races on strength alone. (2) Rowing is a sport that takes place on rivers and lakes. (3) Early in the story, Mei pulls her oar harder than anyone else, and the coach tells her, "Your power is real, but right now it is fighting the boat." (4) This comment shows that Mei's effort is actually slowing the team down, because she is out of rhythm with the other rowers. (5) Mei is frustrated and spends a whole practice "glaring at the back of Tessa's head," blaming her teammate for the uneven strokes.

(6) The turning point comes during a foggy morning practice when Mei cannot see the shore. (7) With nothing else to watch, she listens to the oars and notices that the boat glides fastest when every blade enters the water at the same moment. (8) ____, she stops forcing each stroke and begins matching Tessa's timing. (9) The story ends with the crew finishing a race in second place, and Mei realizes she is "smiling at a loss for the first time." (10) Delgado also describes the bright yellow paint on the team's boat.

(11) Mei learns a lot in this story.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
where public.passages.status = 'draft';
