   $q$Which revision of sentence 11 would best conclude the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mei's smile after a loss shows that she now measures success by how well the crew moves together, not by her own strength.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Stories about sports are popular with readers because many people enjoy watching athletes compete.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-generalization"},{"text":"Mei will probably become the captain of the team next year and lead the crew to a championship.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-prediction"},{"text":"Mei's crew finishes the final race of the story in second place after a long season of practice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-without-analysis"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Mei's smile after a loss shows that she now measures success by how well the crew moves together, not by her own strength.$q$, $q$The best conclusion uses the final quotation to show how Mei's idea of success has changed, tying back to the claim. The choice about becoming captain predicts events that the story never describes.$q$, 'draft', '208778e9-eda2-5ea7-bd39-41e7bfa0a4e1')
