  ('ff3643a1-ce11-5f87-8301-5e982543ca9f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The draft never states a clear claim near the beginning. Which sentence, added after sentence 1, would best state one?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Moreno's evidence shows that turning off tower lights at night sharply reduces the number of migrating birds harmed downtown.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Moreno's article is about office buildings and birds in a city called Port Winslow.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"},{"text":"Office towers in large cities use a great deal of electricity for lights and heating.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"Songbirds are some of the most beautiful animals, and everyone should learn to identify them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-analysis"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Moreno's evidence shows that turning off tower lights at night sharply reduces the number of migrating birds harmed downtown.$q$, $q$The draft's evidence, the drop from 31 to 9 harmed birds, supports a claim that dark towers protect migrating birds. The choice naming the article's subject identifies a topic but makes no point to prove.$q$, 'draft', 'be021c9d-19ba-5312-9674-c15646472be0')
