   $q$Which sentence should replace sentence 2 to state a claim about the poem that the draft supports?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Every family should save its old clothes instead of giving them away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-analysis"},{"text":"Sewing a quilt by hand takes many weeks of careful and patient work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"Kahale uses the quilt to show that family memories can be kept safe and carried into the present.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Kahale's poem describes a quilt that a grandmother made out of clothing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Kahale uses the quilt to show that family memories can be kept safe and carried into the present.$q$, $q$The draft argues that the patches stand for people and memories that still comfort the speaker, so this claim fits. The choice describing the quilt only summarizes the poem's subject without making a point.$q$, 'draft', '5ed646ac-f522-5ec4-9ea2-1669a5d10f19')
