-- Passage wg10-writing-with-evidence-p07
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('2c3ba757-29e3-50d1-9750-e68f0936d7e4', 'wg10-writing-with-evidence-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Draft: Recess Before Lunch$q$, $q$(1) In his article "Play First, Eat Second," nutrition researcher Sanjay Mehta reports on a year-long study at four elementary schools in Fairhaven County. (2) Two of the schools moved recess so that it came before lunch, while the other two kept recess after lunch. (3) Mehta's team weighed the food left on students' trays every Friday. (4) At the schools with recess first, students threw away 30 percent less fruit and vegetables than students at the other schools. (5) Mehta suggests that children who eat right before recess hurry through lunch to get outside, often leaving their vegetables behind.

(6) The study also includes evidence from the cafeteria staff. (7) One lunch monitor told Mehta's team that, after the change, students "actually sat down and ate instead of watching the clock." (8) ____, the schools that switched reported fewer students visiting the nurse with stomachaches in the afternoon. (9) Fairhaven County is well known for its apple orchards. (10) These details show that the order of the school day can shape how well students eat.

(11) Schools should think about recess.$q$, 'draft')
