        '9-12', $q$Evening Hours at the Corwin Library$q$, $q$(1) The Corwin Public Library currently closes at 6:00 on weekday evenings, just as many working adults and high school students finally have time to visit. (2) The library is a pretty cool place. (3) In a survey of 410 residents conducted by the library's own advisory board, 57 percent said they had skipped a visit in the past month because the building was already closed. (4) Students are affected most sharply, since many hold part-time jobs or attend practices that end after 5:30. (5) Extended hours would also give residents without home internet a quiet place to complete job applications and coursework. (6) The library's reading room was renovated in 1998 with oak shelving donated by a local mill.

(7) Critics of the proposal point out that staying open three additional hours each night would raise staffing costs by roughly 14 percent. (8) This is a legitimate concern for a library whose budget has not grown in four years. (9) The library could open three hours later on weekday mornings, when its own records show that fewer than a dozen patrons typically enter before 10:00. (10) Shifting hours rather than adding them would keep staffing costs nearly level while serving far more people.

(11) Anyway, people who say the library should keep its hours just do not get it. (12) So that is why the hours should change.$q$, 'draft')
