  ('f5fbf4e1-01db-52dc-98ce-00babe559764', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-argument-writing'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Sentence (6) is undeveloped. Which revision best turns it into relevant support for the claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Paper for printed books is made from trees, which grow in forests around the world.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Printed books are also heavy: the school nurse found that many students carry backpacks well above the weight recommended for their size.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Some students prefer backpacks with wheels, while others like shoulder straps.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic"},{"text":"Everyone knows that heavy books are annoying to carry around all day long.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-generalization"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Printed books are also heavy: the school nurse found that many students carry backpacks well above the weight recommended for their size.$q$, $q$The correct revision adds specific evidence that connects book weight to a real problem for students. The choice about heavy books being "annoying" appeals to what "everyone knows" instead of offering evidence.$q$, 'draft', '22a42c20-37e4-50da-bf6b-fa65ac05b899')
