insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1da3ac6d-cafc-54ab-b5b7-20736871f430', 'wg11-argument-writing-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Uncovering Fenwick Creek$q$, $q$(1) For nearly ninety years, Fenwick Creek has flowed through a concrete pipe beneath the parking lots of downtown Haldane. (2) The city council should fund a project to "daylight" the creek by removing a 600-meter section of pipe and restoring an open channel with planted banks. (3) Buried streams carry runoff quickly but cannot absorb heavy rain, and the Fenwick pipe has overflowed onto Market Street four times in the past decade. (4) An open channel with wide banks would hold more water during storms, reducing the flooding that has damaged nearby shops. (5) A restored creek would also cool the surrounding blocks on summer afternoons, according to temperature readings taken by students at Haldane Community College.

(6) The strongest objection is cost, since the project is estimated at $9 million. (7) The loss of roughly 140 parking spaces also worries downtown business owners. (8) These concerns deserve a serious answer. (9) State flood-prevention grants could cover about half of the cost, and the city already spends nearly $400,000 a year repairing the existing pipe. (10) A new parking structure two blocks away, which the city has already planned, would replace most of the lost spaces.

(11) Fish are cool to look at too. (12) Daylighting Fenwick Creek would protect Market Street from floods, cool downtown and, over time, cost less than repairing a failing pipe forever.$q$, 'draft')
