insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('175c0575-5051-5d8e-99de-5188c2c476d4', 'wg11-argument-writing-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Video Review in the Playoffs$q$, $q$(1) In last year's Tri-County girls' soccer semifinal, a goal that video later showed was clearly offside decided the match. (2) The Tri-County Athletic League should allow limited video review during playoff games for goals and penalty decisions only. (3) High school referees work without video assistants, and even skilled officials miss fast plays seen from poor angles. (4) Most playoff games are already filmed by both schools and by the league's own streaming crew, so the footage exists. (5) A league review of the 2024 playoffs counted six goals that video showed were awarded in error, and four of those changed the outcome.

(6) Opponents raise two concerns. (7) First, they argue that stopping play to review footage would slow the game and frustrate players. (8) Limiting review to goals and penalties, with a two-minute maximum per check, would keep stoppages brief and rare. (9) Second, some coaches warn that review would undermine respect for referees. (10) Video review would support referees by giving them a way to correct honest mistakes rather than defend them.

(11) Soccer is the most popular sport in the world. (12) Given that the footage already exists and the stakes of playoff games are high, the league should adopt limited review beginning next season.$q$, 'draft')
