   $q$Which revision of sentence (12) best maintains a formal style?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Restoring a darker sky would also return a view of the stars that most residents now lack.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Stars are really pretty, so obviously everyone deserves to see them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-informal-tone"},{"text":"Everybody loves looking at stars, and that is simply a fact.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Stars are nice to look at in a lot of different ways.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-wording"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Restoring a darker sky would also return a view of the stars that most residents now lack.$q$, $q$The correct revision uses precise, formal language and ties back to the contrast in sentence (1). The other choices keep casual wording, overgeneralize, or stay vague.$q$, 'draft', '78c7f5e9-36b1-5db0-a259-60496079ef53')
