   $q$Which sentence about a history lesson uses capital letters correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"In History class, Professor Okafor explained how the Industrial Revolution changed the textile trade.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"school-subject-capitalized"},{"text":"In history class, professor Okafor explained how the Industrial Revolution changed the textile trade.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"title-before-name-lowercase"},{"text":"In history class, Professor Okafor explained how the industrial revolution changed the textile trade.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"historical-period-lowercase"},{"text":"In history class, Professor Okafor explained how the Industrial Revolution changed the textile trade.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$In history class, Professor Okafor explained how the Industrial Revolution changed the textile trade.$q$, $q$"Professor" is capitalized as a title directly before a name, and "Industrial Revolution" is the name of a historical period. "History" is a general school subject, not a language, so it stays lowercase.$q$, 'draft', null)
