   $q$Which sentence correctly punctuates the list of tour stops?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The choir's summer tour stopped in Lagos; Nigeria, Accra; Ghana, and Dakar; Senegal.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolons-misplaced"},{"text":"The choir's summer tour stopped in: Lagos, Nigeria; Accra, Ghana; and Dakar, Senegal.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-after-preposition"},{"text":"The choir's summer tour stopped in Lagos, Nigeria; Accra, Ghana; and Dakar, Senegal.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The choir's summer tour stopped in Lagos, Nigeria, Accra, Ghana, and Dakar, Senegal.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"commas-only-in-complex-series"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The choir's summer tour stopped in Lagos, Nigeria; Accra, Ghana; and Dakar, Senegal.$q$, $q$Each item in the series already contains a comma between city and country, so semicolons separate the items to keep them clear. With commas only, a reader cannot tell where one stop ends and the next begins.$q$, 'draft', null)
