   $q$Which sentence correctly punctuates the nonessential clause?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The observatory, which, sits on a ridge above the valley, opens to the public each Friday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-after-relative-pronoun"},{"text":"The observatory which sits on a ridge above the valley, opens to the public each Friday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-opening-comma"},{"text":"The observatory, which sits on a ridge above the valley opens to the public each Friday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-closing-comma"},{"text":"The observatory, which sits on a ridge above the valley, opens to the public each Friday.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The observatory, which sits on a ridge above the valley, opens to the public each Friday.$q$, $q$"Which sits on a ridge above the valley" adds extra information about the observatory, so it needs a comma at each end. With only the first comma, the clause runs into the main verb "opens."$q$, 'draft', null)
