   $q$Which sentence about the astronomy club is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Having repaired, the cracked lens the astronomy club members reopened the telescope for night viewing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splits-phrase"},{"text":"Having repaired the cracked lens, the astronomy club members reopened the telescope for night viewing.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Having repaired the cracked lens; the astronomy club members reopened the telescope for night viewing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-after-phrase"},{"text":"Having repaired the cracked lens the astronomy club members, reopened the telescope for night viewing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-misplaced"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Having repaired the cracked lens, the astronomy club members reopened the telescope for night viewing.$q$, $q$The introductory participial phrase "Having repaired the cracked lens" ends before the subject, so the comma goes after "lens." A semicolon cannot follow a phrase because it must separate two independent clauses.$q$, 'draft', null)
