   $q$Which sentence about the pottery sale is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"At the pottery sale, Amara bought three, small, ceramic bowls for the family table.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-between-cumulative-adjectives"},{"text":"At the pottery sale, Amara bought three small ceramic, bowls for the family table.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-before-noun"},{"text":"At the pottery sale, Amara bought three small, ceramic bowls for the family table.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-between-cumulative-adjectives"},{"text":"At the pottery sale, Amara bought three small ceramic bowls for the family table.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$At the pottery sale, Amara bought three small ceramic bowls for the family table.$q$, $q$"Three small ceramic" are cumulative adjectives: each one builds on the words after it, and they cannot be reordered or joined with "and," so no commas are used. Placing a comma between "small" and "ceramic" treats them as coordinate adjectives when they are not.$q$, 'draft', null)
