   $q$Which sentence about the film festival is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The outdoor film festival was postponed; because the stage had flooded overnight.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-before-dependent-clause"},{"text":"The outdoor film festival was postponed because the stage had flooded overnight.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The outdoor film festival was postponed because, the stage had flooded overnight.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-after-subordinator"},{"text":"The outdoor film festival was postponed: because the stage had flooded overnight.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-before-dependent-clause"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The outdoor film festival was postponed because the stage had flooded overnight.$q$, $q$"Because the stage had flooded overnight" is a dependent clause that follows the main clause, so no punctuation is needed before it. A semicolon must join two independent clauses, and this clause cannot stand alone.$q$, 'draft', null)
