  ('aa84332d-d864-550b-9367-bdb80f60ca76', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-capitalization-punctuation'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which sentence about the arts committee is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The arts committee chose three finalists: Ines Varga, a sculptor from Duluth; Tomas Achebe, a weaver; and Lin Park, a potter.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The arts committee chose three finalists; Ines Varga, a sculptor from Duluth; Tomas Achebe, a weaver; and Lin Park, a potter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-for-colon"},{"text":"The arts committee chose three finalists: Ines Varga; a sculptor from Duluth, Tomas Achebe; a weaver, and Lin Park; a potter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolons-misplaced"},{"text":"The arts committee chose three finalists, Ines Varga, a sculptor from Duluth, Tomas Achebe, a weaver, and Lin Park, a potter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"commas-only-in-complex-series"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The arts committee chose three finalists: Ines Varga, a sculptor from Duluth; Tomas Achebe, a weaver; and Lin Park, a potter.$q$, $q$A colon after the complete clause introduces the list, and because each item contains a comma before its description, semicolons separate the items. Using a semicolon in place of the colon wrongly treats the list as an independent clause.$q$, 'draft', null)
