   $q$Which sentence about the suspension bridge is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The suspension bridge, which was completed in 1932, still carries traffic; its steel cables, however, were replaced last year.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The suspension bridge, which was completed in 1932, still carries traffic; its steel cables; however, were replaced last year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-for-comma"},{"text":"The suspension bridge, which was completed in 1932, still carries traffic, its steel cables, however, were replaced last year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice"},{"text":"The suspension bridge which was completed in 1932, still carries traffic; its steel cables, however, were replaced last year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-opening-comma"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The suspension bridge, which was completed in 1932, still carries traffic; its steel cables, however, were replaced last year.$q$, $q$The nonessential clause about 1932 is set off by two commas, a semicolon joins the two independent clauses, and "however" interrupts the second clause, so commas surround it. Replacing the semicolon with a comma creates a comma splice between the two clauses.$q$, 'draft', null)
