   $q$Which sentence correctly punctuates the parenthetical reference at the end?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The canal shortened the trip between the lake ports and the coast by several days (see the map on page 12).","is_correct":true},{"text":"The canal shortened the trip between the lake ports and the coast by several days, (see the map on page 12).","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-before-parentheses"},{"text":"The canal shortened the trip between the lake ports and the coast by several days. (see the map on page 12)","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sentence-ends-before-parentheses"},{"text":"The canal shortened the trip between the lake ports and the coast by several days (see the map on page 12.)","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"period-inside-parentheses"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The canal shortened the trip between the lake ports and the coast by several days (see the map on page 12).$q$, $q$When a parenthetical note is part of the sentence, the sentence's period goes after the closing parenthesis. Putting the period inside the parentheses would only be correct if the parenthetical were a complete sentence of its own.$q$, 'draft', null)
