   $q$The report has no conclusion. Which sentence, added after sentence 12, would best conclude it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Some trees live for more than a thousand years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-detail"},{"text":"Because each ring records a single year, tree rings allow researchers to answer historical questions and recover climate history that people never wrote down.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Tree rings are cool, and everyone should count the rings on a stump.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-opinion"},{"text":"Tree rings are formed by pale spring cells and dark summer cells.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because each ring records a single year, tree rings allow researchers to answer historical questions and recover climate history that people never wrote down.$q$, $q$The correct sentence connects the annual nature of rings to both uses described in paragraphs 3 and 4 and explains why that matters. The sentence about spring and summer cells only repeats sentence 2.$q$, 'draft', '6b2c1d2d-62f0-5ef8-bff4-c4c6c1938a70')
