   $q$The writer is considering moving sentence 5 so that it follows sentence 7. Should the writer make this change?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Yes, because sentence 5 introduces a topic unrelated to matching patterns.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-relationship"},{"text":"Yes, because sentence 5 states a conclusion and belongs at the end of the paragraph.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-function"},{"text":"No, because sentence 5 is the only sentence in the report that contains a definition.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-reason"},{"text":"No, because sentences 6 and 7 depend on the idea that ring width varies with climate, which sentence 5 establishes.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$No, because sentences 6 and 7 depend on the idea that ring width varies with climate, which sentence 5 establishes.$q$, $q$Shared patterns of wide and narrow rings only make sense once readers know that climate controls ring width, so sentence 5 must come first. The choice about definitions gives the wrong reason, since sentence 4 also contains a definition.$q$, 'draft', '6b2c1d2d-62f0-5ef8-bff4-c4c6c1938a70')
