-- Passage wg11-narrative-writing-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('2467747a-cf2a-53b6-97a6-bd364b396dca', 'wg11-narrative-writing-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-narrative-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Seat Three$q$, $q$(1) At five-forty in the morning, the river was the color of pewter, and mist hung so low over the water that I could not see the far bank. (2) Our boat, a long white shell we called the Heron, sat on its rack while the eight of us stretched in silence. (3) I was rowing in seat three for the first time, replacing Danielle, who had sprained a wrist the week before. (4) Our coxswain, Priya, would steer and call the strokes from the stern.

(5) For two weeks I had been late on the catch, dropping my oar into the water a fraction of a second after everyone else. (6) Each time, the boat lurched slightly to one side. (7) Nobody said anything, but I could feel the hull wobble and knew it was my fault.

(8) The race started. (9) Priya's voice cut through the mist: "Lengthen! Stay together!" (10) By the halfway marker we were even with the crew from Lakeview. (11) My legs burned, and my lungs felt as if they were full of sand. (12) Then I stopped watching my own oar and watched the back of Marco's shoulders in seat four instead. (13) When Marco moved, I moved. (14) The Heron stopped wobbling and seemed to lift, gliding between strokes.

(15) We crossed the line half a length ahead of Lakeview. (16) We were very happy.$q$, 'draft')
